  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Reborn covers many character fantasies involving returning from death, producing a character that’s resilient and unlikely to die a second time. Whether you’re more machine than man now, reanimated by mad science, a ghost possessing your own body, or some other variety of not dead anymore, you’re "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In combat, Advantage on Death Saving Throws makes falling to 0 hit points much less scary. Taken as a whole, the Reborn is a great option for players who consider themselves unlucky and who need some mathematical backup, as well as for players who tend to get themselves killed a lot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This guide is for the 2024 DnD 5.5 rules. For the 2014 DnD 5e rules, see our "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "DnD 5e Reborn Lineage Guide",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/races/reborn/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
