    {
      "sectionId": "section-changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules",
      "heading": "Changes from the 2014 DnD 5e Rules to the 2024 DnD 5.5 Rules",
      "sourceAnchor": "changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ancestral Legacy has been removed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Deathless Nature has been broken up into multiple features, and the wording has been made consistent with the 5.5 rules. Resistance to disease and poison has been removed and replaced by Strange Endurance."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Knowledge from a Past Life has been updated to work like many other expendable dice buffs like Bardic Inspiration; it is now used when you fail a roll rather than when you initially attempt the roll"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Strange Endurance is new"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Reborn Traits",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "text": "Size"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Medium. There are nearly no meaningful distinctions\n\t\tbetween Small and Medium size. Small characters can be swallowed whole more\n\t\teasily and have lower carrying capacity, but can ride smaller mounts."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Speed"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Normal."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Escaped Death"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": It’s already hard to die in DnD 5.5, but this makes it nearly certain that you won’t die as long a everything leaves you alone once you hit 0 hp."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Everlasting"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful because these threats are rare in the vast majority of campaigns."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Knowledge from a Past Life"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Excellent support on ability checks."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Strange Endurance"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Poison will be the most consistently usefful, but it’s also the easiest to find somewhere else, and you can’t change your choice once you’ve made it."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Reborn Classes",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes",
      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Artificer doesn’t get any unique benefits from the Reborn. Their durability is still good for front-line builds like the Armorer and the Battle Smith, and Knowledge From a Past Life will help with ability checks, but there’s no specific synergy here."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The reborn’s durability works very well for the Barbarian. Lean into their high risk, high reward design, confident in knowing that if you do fall to 0 hit points, Escaped Death will tilt the odds of your Death Saves heavily toward survival so that you can fight another day. Knowledge from a Past Life will help with ability checks, which may help with your poor skill options."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Between Jack of All Trades and Knowledge From a Past Life, you can be very successful with skills without worrying much about Proficiency. The Reborn’s additional durability may also help with the Bard’s relatively poor durability, especially if you’re building for melee."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Cleric doesn’t get any unique benefits from the Reborn. The additional durability is still good for front-line builds, and Knowledge From a Past Life will help with skills, but the Cleric typically isn’t a skill-heavy class."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Druid doesn’t get any unique benefits from the Reborn. The additional durability is still good for front-line builds, and Knowledge From a Past Life will help with skills, but the Druid typically isn’t a skill-heavy class."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Fighter benefits as much as any other front-line build does from the Reborn’s durability. Combining Knowledge from a Past Life with Tactical Mind gives you two options to rescue failed ability checks, and nothing stops you from combining them, so you should rarely fail ability checks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The additional durability is nice, and Knowledge from a Past Life can help with skill checks. It’s not enough to replace Expertise so that you can replace a Rogue, but it helps."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Paladin benefits as much as any other front-line Defender from the Reborn’s durability. Paladins are frequently their party’s Face, but many builds can’t afford 20 Charisma until late in their career, and many will never get there. Without the full Charisma of a Charisma-based build (Bard, etc.). you’re slightly behind those characters with your most important skills. Knowledge from a Past Life will make up the difference between you and characters with better Charisma."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The additional durability is nice, and Knowledge from a Past Life can help with skill checks. It’s not enough to replace Expertise so that you can replace a Rogue, but it helps."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sometimes Expertise just isn’t enough to offset bad rolls, especially before you get Reliable Talent, so Knowledge From the Past provides some extra insurance on important ability checks. Hopefully the extra durability won’t matter much, but many rogues fight in melee despite low AC and hit points compared to other martial classes, so having the extra protection is really nice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With d6 hit dice and no armor, the Sorcerer is extremely frail, so the extra durability is a great comfort. Knowledge From the Past will help with important ability checks, but remember that you can also buff skill checks with spells like Enhance Ability."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While the Warlock isn’t as frail as the Sorcerer or the Wizard, the Reborn’s additional durability still feels nice on the Warlock, especially if you’re going to brave close quarters. Knowledge From the Past will help with ability checks, which is great since the Warlock doesn’t get Enhance Ability."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-2",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With d6 hit dice and no armor, the Sorcerer is extremely frail, so the extra durability is a great comfort. Knowledge From the Past will help with important ability checks, but remember that you can also buff skill checks with spells like Enhance Ability."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
